# Stage 1: prompt the robot. A phrase, or an example image with a box around the object, says WHICH object (its best
# detection in the latest fixed-camera frame); the library (stored example + mesh per target) says WHAT it is. If it
# is a target, that target's Detect sends the prompt's mask from now on. No text and no image: back to the library.
string text                      # e.g. "the yellow bottle"; ignored when an image is given
sensor_msgs/Image image          # example image (rgb8 / bgr8); empty = text prompt
float32[4] bbox                  # the object in that image, x0 y0 x1 y1 (px); all 0 = the whole image
---
bool found                       # the prompt matched something in the frame
string target                    # the target it was taken for; "" = nothing the robot can pick
string label                     # the target, else what the text check calls it
float32 score                    # the prompt's detection score
float32[4] bbox                  # in the camera image (px)
string message
